// Package gotestruntime is what the harness gotest generates calls: it opens
// a suite, holds its fixtures, runs its methods under their budgets and ends
// them when the run is stopped.
//
// It is for generated code only. Write tests against package gotest; nothing
// here is meant to be called from one. The API is append-only, so a harness
// generated by an older gotest compiles against a newer runtime: names are
// added, never changed, and the ones in deprecated.go stay for that reason.
package gotestruntime
